        {
          "id": "IC_kwDOE3b6388AAAABMu9TnQ",
          "author": {
            "login": "wbniv"
          },
          "authorAssociation": "CONTRIBUTOR",
          "body": "Updated (`1824492` \u2192 `edc9bbd`, amended): added `coalesce-rotate-ac-no-pessimize.ll`, pinning the cost side \u2014 common straight-line shift chains (`i8`/`i16` `<< 2`) keep their tight `asl`/`rol` form with the guard in place, byte-identical to the unguarded output. Also rewrote the PR body: a precise scope section (what the guard fixes vs. the downstream RA behavior it deliberately doesn't change), exact Csmith accounting, why no end-to-end miscompile test is extractable, and dropped the embedded patch listing that had drifted from the real diff. Fix unchanged.",
          "createdAt": "2026-08-01T03:07:32Z",
          "includesCreatedEdit": false,
          "isMinimized": false,
          "minimizedReason": "",
          "reactionGroups": [],
          "url": "https://github.com/llvm-mos/llvm-mos/pull/578#issuecomment-5149512605",
          "viewerDidAuthor": true
        },
        {
          "id": "IC_kwDOE3b6388AAAABQIKcKA",
          "author": {
            "login": "mysterymath"
          },
          "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
          "body": "Yeah, reading the PR description, I reheheaaally don't like that this is papering over a bug elsewhere. That might *work*, but we really should get to the bottom of why this is happening. Especially since fixing upstream bugs is part of the game, *and* since I'm an upstream llvm contributor, and if we fix something wrong there, well, that's good for everyone.",
          "createdAt": "2026-08-22T02:05:36Z",
          "includesCreatedEdit": true,
          "isMinimized": false,
          "minimizedReason": "",
          "reactionGroups": [],
          "url": "https://github.com/llvm-mos/llvm-mos/pull/578#issuecomment-5377268776",
          "viewerDidAuthor": false
        },
        {
          "id": "IC_kwDOE3b6388AAAABUWKy_Q",
          "author": {
            "login": "wbniv"
          },
          "authorAssociation": "CONTRIBUTOR",
          "body": "You were right, and it wasn't the coalescer or RA at all. Got to the bottom of it; the branch and description are replaced (`edc9bbd` \u2192 `b474922`).\n\nThe coalescer's join and greedy's allocation were both correct \u2014 the rewriter emits the `A = COPY Y` restore at the loop header exactly as it should. What eats it is `MOSCopyOpt`: it forwards that copy away (legitimately \u2014 the value is already in Y), which changes the register that has to stay live around the back edge from Y to A. Then its liveness update is a *single* post-order pass over the blocks, which visits the latch before the header, so the header's new `$a` live-in never propagates to the latch. `mos-late-opt` later sees A dead at the latch and uses it as scratch when lowering the `CmpBrZero` \u2014 the stale-A read that looked like an RA bug from the outside. Pass-by-pass evidence in the description.\n\nFix is a `fullyRecomputeLiveIns` before the dead-copy cleanup so live-ins reach a fixed point first. The `shouldCoalesce` guard and both its tests are gone; ordinary rotate coalescing is back on. It's entirely inside the target pass \u2014 nothing upstream was wrong, so nothing to send upstream, sorry.\n\nRegression is a reduced MIR loop: fails on both prefixes without the fix (latch lacks `$a`; the bad `LDImag8` reload appears), and the original CRC demo goes from a host/ROM mismatch to agreement. The recompute costs +0.8% retired instructions across a 176-file corpus, worst case +2.4% on a loop-dense kernel.\n",
          "createdAt": "2026-09-14T07:15:22Z",
          "includesCreatedEdit": false,
          "isMinimized": false,
          "minimizedReason": "",
          "reactionGroups": [],
          "url": "https://github.com/llvm-mos/llvm-mos/pull/578#issuecomment-5660390141",
          "viewerDidAuthor": true
        }
      ],
