      "title": "[MOS] Recompute loop liveness after copy forwarding",
      "updatedAt": "2026-09-25T01:26:53Z",
      "url": "https://github.com/llvm-mos/llvm-mos/pull/578"
    },
    {
      "repository": "llvm-mos/llvm-mos",
      "comments": [
        {
          "id": "IC_kwDOE3b6388AAAABMurz1A",
          "author": {
            "login": "wbniv"
          },
          "authorAssociation": "CONTRIBUTOR",
          "body": "Two updates after a post-hoc review of this PR:\n\n1. **7eedb14 hardens the guard.** The bare `continue` was correct only because no current non-GPR `LDImm` destination aliases `A`/`X`/`Y` \u2014 an invariant the register file happens to satisfy rather than one the code enforces. The follow-up commit invalidates any tracked GPR the instruction modifies before continuing, mirroring the invalidation the loop already performs for non-`LDImm` instructions. Behaviour-identical for all current inputs (the checks are dead code until something widens `LDImm`'s destination class further); all four `late-opt*.mir` tests pass unchanged, including the transparency case pinning that a `TAX` rewrite still fires across `$rc2 = LDImm 7`. For the record: the `TA` handler at the top of the same loop has the identical switch-then-store shape, but nothing widens `TA`'s destination class, so it is deliberately left untouched.\n\n2. **The description's live-byte claim was corrected.** The original text said eight simultaneously-live bytes was the smallest count that reliably forces a constant into an imaginary register, and that four stayed in the GPRs. Re-measured (MIR captured with `-mllvm -stop-before=mos-late-opt`, fed to an unfixed `llc -run-pass=mos-late-opt`): **three** live bytes crash at every level above `-O0`, and **two** crash at `-Oz`. The 8-variable repro stands as posted \u2014 the bug is easier to hit than the original text claimed, not harder.",
          "createdAt": "2026-08-01T02:28:13Z",
          "includesCreatedEdit": false,
          "isMinimized": false,
          "minimizedReason": "",
          "reactionGroups": [],
          "url": "https://github.com/llvm-mos/llvm-mos/pull/584#issuecomment-5149225940",
          "viewerDidAuthor": true
        },
        {
          "id": "IC_kwDOE3b6388AAAABMu9TzA",
          "author": {
            "login": "wbniv"
          },
          "authorAssociation": "CONTRIBUTOR",
          "body": "Updated (`7eedb14` \u2192 `3ce98fe`): new commit hardens the sibling `TA` handler in `combineLdImm`, which has the same switch-then-unconditional-store shape the LDImm fix guards \u2014 unreachable today (`TA`'s destination class is XY-only), but this function is where \"unreachable today\" already failed once, so it now falls through to the generic invalidation instead of trusting the switch. No behavior change for any current input; all four late-opt tests green. Body re-synced with the shipped defensive-invalidation guard.",
