      "title": "[MOS] Fix non-GPR immediate loads in mos-late-opt",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-05T22:55:19Z",
      "url": "https://github.com/llvm-mos/llvm-mos/pull/584"
    },
    {
      "repository": "llvm-mos/llvm-mos",
      "comments": [
        {
          "id": "IC_kwDOE3b6388AAAABOEhu8g",
          "author": {
            "login": "johnwbyrd"
          },
          "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
          "body": "The major concern about such a change is how the disassembler would deal with it.  Strictly, it changes disassembly from being deterministic to non-deterministic.  I could buy off on this, if disassembly always ends up being the Implied version.  Would be nice to see some round-trip tests added to prove that this breaks no one else.",
          "createdAt": "2026-08-10T10:59:11Z",
          "includesCreatedEdit": false,
          "isMinimized": false,
          "minimizedReason": "",
          "reactionGroups": [],
          "url": "https://github.com/llvm-mos/llvm-mos/pull/586#issuecomment-5239238386",
          "viewerDidAuthor": false
        },
        {
          "id": "IC_kwDOE3b6388AAAABRgoPZw",
          "author": {
            "login": "mysterymath"
          },
          "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
          "body": "> The major concern about such a change is how the disassembler would deal with it. Strictly, it changes disassembly from being deterministic to non-deterministic. I could buy off on this, if disassembly always ends up being the Implied version. Would be nice to see some round-trip tests added to prove that this breaks no one else.\r\n\r\nI'd be curious what the prior art is here; are other disassemblers (particularly da65) willing to infer a tag for `BRK`? In the absence of compelling prior art, I'd expect `brk #66` to be purely syntactic sugar in the assembler for `brk .byte 66`. I'd never expect the disassembler to produce a `brk #66` accordingly; it's not in the business of lifting the disassembly to a higher level.\r\n\r\nAlong those lines, I'm broadly in favor, if just because `ca65` supports this.",
          "createdAt": "2026-08-30T16:57:11Z",
          "includesCreatedEdit": false,
          "isMinimized": false,
          "minimizedReason": "",
          "reactionGroups": [],
          "url": "https://github.com/llvm-mos/llvm-mos/pull/586#issuecomment-5470031719",
