      "title": "[MOS] Add the COP mnemonic with a mandatory signature operand",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-05T22:55:38Z",
      "url": "https://github.com/llvm-mos/llvm-mos/pull/588"
    },
    {
      "repository": "llvm-mos/llvm-mos",
      "comments": [
        {
          "id": "IC_kwDOE3b6388AAAABUSiO8g",
          "author": {
            "login": "wbniv"
          },
          "authorAssociation": "CONTRIBUTOR",
          "body": "This is exactly the fix pushed here: `CmpZero` is now `isTerminator = true`, and `lowerCmpZeros` scans `MBB.terminators()` instead of the whole block. The original reproducer (a normal instruction after `CmpZero`) is no longer reachable at all \u2014 the verifier itself rejects it, so it's replaced with a negative test (`cmpzero-terminator-invalid.mir`) that asserts exactly that rejection, plus a positive test with adjacent `CmpZero`s that must fold and lower independently.\n\nWhile making the pseudo a terminator, I also found and fixed the bug the original PR's reproducer was standing in for: `lowerCmpZeros` shared the function's `Changed` accumulator as the per-`CmpZero` \"did this one fold\" flag, so once any `CmpZero` in a block folded, every later one took the early continue and was never lowered \u2014 silently dropping a flag test, since a surviving `CmpZero` is legal MIR and the asm printer emits nothing for it. That's a separate `Folded` flag now, with `Changed` set correctly on the dead-comparison erase path too.\n\nUpdated branch incoming.\n",
          "createdAt": "2026-09-13T22:24:42Z",
          "includesCreatedEdit": false,
          "isMinimized": false,
          "minimizedReason": "",
          "reactionGroups": [],
          "url": "https://github.com/llvm-mos/llvm-mos/pull/589#issuecomment-5656579826",
          "viewerDidAuthor": true
        }
      ],
      "headRefOid": "9aead7afaa4a13f4e7151e2b62adbc0b6937a018",
      "mergeCommit": {
        "oid": "f24948c7d1a4b9f162d4d0192ccceecab1e441ff"
      },
      "mergedAt": "2026-10-05T22:55:59Z",
      "number": 589,
      "reviewDecision": "APPROVED",
      "reviews": [
